Description: Update obsolete autotools macros for automake >= 1.13 / autoconf >= 2.70

The tarball ships no pre-generated configure; the recipe bootstraps
with autoreconf (automake 1.18 / autoconf 2.72 era). Upstream
configure.in still uses macros removed or deprecated there:

- AM_CONFIG_HEADER was removed in automake 1.13 -> AC_CONFIG_HEADERS
- AM_PROG_LIBTOOL is a deprecated libtool alias -> LT_INIT
- old-style AC_OUTPUT(Makefile) with arguments -> AC_CONFIG_FILES + AC_OUTPUT

Behavior is unchanged; only macro spelling is modernized.

--- a/configure.in
+++ b/configure.in
@@ -6,13 +6,13 @@
 dnl AC_LIBTOOL_DLOPEN
 
 AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE
-AM_CONFIG_HEADER(config.h)
+AC_CONFIG_HEADERS([config.h])
 
 AC_CONFIG_MACRO_DIR([m4])
 
 AC_PROG_CC
 
-AM_PROG_LIBTOOL
+LT_INIT
 AC_PROG_MAKE_SET
 
 dnl intitialization
@@ -251,5 +251,6 @@
    AC_DEFINE(HAVE_SENDFILE, 1, [Define if your system has the sendfile system call])
 fi
 
-AC_OUTPUT(Makefile)
-
+AC_CONFIG_FILES([Makefile])
+AC_OUTPUT
+
